<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Leong Prop up on joint venture talk.</title>
<headline>Hong Leong Prop up on joint venture talk.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian over-the-counter stock Hong Leong Properties Bhd saw its volume surge in mid-morning on talk of a joint venture with publisher Nanyang Press (M) Bhd, dealers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>At 0301 GMT, Hong Leong Properties was up Singapore $0.09 to S$1.88 and topped the actives with 1.9 million shares.  </p>
<p>Dealers said there were also rumours of a restructuring within the Hong Leong group of companies. Hong Leong companies listed on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange (KLSE) were also rising.</p>
<p>At 0305 GMT, Nanyang Press rose 0.55 ringgit to 9.90 ringgit on the KLSE.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
